.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-gpg 1  "git-gpg 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
git\-gpg \- Git secret management using pure Rust OpenPGP
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-gpg\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Git secret management using pure Rust OpenPGP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
git\-gpg\-init(1)
Initialize git\-gpg in the current repository
.TP
git\-gpg\-import(1)
Import your private key(s) into the git\-gpg key store
.TP
git\-gpg\-trust(1)
Establish trust for a repository by verifying the owner\*(Aqs signing key
.TP
git\-gpg\-tell(1)
Add a collaborator\*(Aqs public key to the keyring
.TP
git\-gpg\-removeperson(1)
Remove a collaborator from the keyring
.TP
git\-gpg\-add(1)
Add a file to be encrypted
.TP
git\-gpg\-remove(1)
Remove a file from encryption tracking
.TP
git\-gpg\-list(1)
List all tracked files
.TP
git\-gpg\-hide(1)
Hide \- encrypt all tracked files
.TP
git\-gpg\-reveal(1)
Reveal \- decrypt all tracked files
.TP
git\-gpg\-cat(1)
Cat \- decrypt a single tracked file to stdout
.TP
git\-gpg\-unhide(1)
Unhide \- decrypt a single tracked file back to plaintext and delete its ciphertext
.TP
git\-gpg\-changes(1)
Changes \- report where plaintext differs from the last hidden version
.TP
git\-gpg\-show\-repo\-id(1)
Show the repository ID
.TP
git\-gpg\-whoami(1)
Show your identity
.TP
git\-gpg\-verify\-keyring(1)
Verify the keyring signature
.TP
git\-gpg\-list\-keys(1)
List all keys in the keyring (requires a verified keyring signature)
.TP
git\-gpg\-clean(1)
Clean \- remove all git\-gpg metadata
.TP
git\-gpg\-completions(1)
Emit a shell completion script for the given shell to stdout
.TP
git\-gpg\-manpages(1)
Write roff man pages (git\-gpg.1 plus one per subcommand) to a directory
.TP
git\-gpg\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
